# Iframe embed constraint

This site is not a standalone tab. It is framed by another site (Cargo / kaik.pictures). Treat the iframe viewport as the only window we own.

## Layout and scroll

- Fill the iframe: `html, body` are `width/height: 100%`.
- Course landing: `body` is `overflow: hidden`. Scroll lives on `[data-scroll-root].viewport`, never on `window`.
- Admin (`body.admin`): scroll on `body` with `overscroll-behavior: contain`.
- `position: fixed` UI (panel, deck, toasts, popovers) stays **outside** the scroll root, as a sibling, so it sticks to the iframe viewport.
- Size against `--frame-w` / `--frame-h` (set from `innerWidth` / `innerHeight`). Do not rely on `100vh` / `100vw` alone.
- Keep `overscroll-behavior: contain` so wheel/touch does not chain to the parent page.
- Parent must give the iframe a real height (typically `100vh` of the host). Do not auto-grow the iframe to content height — the card flight needs an internal scroller.

## Navigation and browser APIs

- Internal `#hash` links scroll the scroll root, not `window`.
- External links (`kaik.pictures`, forms, etc.) use `target="_top"` so they leave the iframe.
- Never break out with `window.top.location` unless the user is following an external link.
- `localStorage` / cookies may be blocked in a third-party iframe — always go through `safeStorage()` in `src/embed.js`.
- Do not set `X-Frame-Options`. Keep `Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors *` on the Vite server so Cargo can frame us.
- Do not add COOP/COEP headers that would refuse framing.

## New pages and features

- Admin, catalog, overlays, modals: they must fit and scroll inside the iframe, not assume a full browser chrome.
- Modals: `position: fixed` relative to the iframe; trap overscroll.
- No `window.open` to same-origin flows that the user expects to see in the embed — stay in-frame unless it is an external destination.
